Error: Jet.InlineAlwaysScrub: `redact` is `#Scrub`, so `#Inline(Always)` cannot expand it
  --> Tests/UI/inline_always_scrub.jet:4:3
    |
  4 | #[Inline(Always), Scrub(PII)]
    |   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
 Why: A `#Scrub` routine reveals a fixed value as a public result, and only its own call keeps that value fixed up to the result; an inlined copy would let the fixed value flow on into the caller's code. `#Inline(Always)` guarantees that every direct call is inlined on every tier, or the program is refused: sema refuses a function that calls itself or closes a cycle of marked calls (Jet.RecursiveInlineAlways), one used as a value (Jet.InlineAlwaysAddressTaken), one over the size ceiling (Jet.InlineAlwaysTooLarge), a `#Scrub` routine (Jet.InlineAlwaysScrub), one that reads `context.trace` (Jet.InlineAlwaysReadsTrace) and one with a foreign body (Jet.InlineAlwaysForeign).
 Fix: Drop `#Inline(Always)`; a `#Scrub` routine stays a call.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.InlineAlwaysScrub
